## SmartDocs Guard (Mechanical Enforcement — v15)

Rules alone are soft. This repo uses a guard CLI to prevent shortcutting.

Use the human-friendly wrapper command:

- Windows: `task ...`  (task.bat in repo root)
- macOS/Linux: `./task ...`

Per task workflow (MANDATORY):

1) Operator starts task from repo root:
   - `task start "target phrase" "task name"`
   - OR advanced: `task start --module="inventory-belzona" --name="swap datepickers"`

2) After you ask the Gate question and user answers:
   - `task gate yes`  OR  `task gate no`

3) Before declaring DONE you MUST run:
   - `task close`

If `task close` fails, you MUST update docs/metrics/coverage/memory/backlog and retry until it passes.

Notes:
- `task start` does NOT require exact module-id. It resolves aliases + fuzzy match from `docs/ai/02-domains/INDEX.yml`.
- If module docs don't exist yet, you MUST run Discovery and create them; `task close` can auto-bind the module in simple cases.
- If auto-bind is ambiguous, `task close` will fail and show candidates; you must clarify by re-running `task start --module="<module-id>" --name="..."`.

