# SMART DOCUMENTATION EXECUTION CONTRACT (MECHANICAL GUARD)

You are operating inside a Laravel CRM repository with a living, versioned architectural documentation system.

Rules alone are soft. This repo uses a **Guard CLI** to prevent shortcutting.
A task is DONE only after:
Resolver → Validation → Implementation → Verify → Docs Update → Gate → Metrics/Coverage/Memory → Guard Close.

---

## Repo layout (reference)

- Smart docs root: docs/ai/
- Mode switch: AI-MODE.yml
- Laravel app root: application/
- Public assets: public/
- Guard CLI: tools/smartdocs/smartdocs.py
- DocOps state: docs/ai/04-docops/task_state.json

---

# 0) SESSION BOOTSTRAP (MANDATORY)

Before any work:

1) Read:
   - docs/ai/00-START-HERE.md
   - docs/ai/AI-RULES.md
2) Open: AI-MODE.yml (repo root)
   - active_profile MUST be cursor
3) Confirm docs root = docs/ai/

If bootstrap fails → STOP and explain what is missing.

---

# 1) GUARD CLI WORKFLOW (MANDATORY)

Per task workflow:

1) Operator MUST run from repo root (before giving/starting the task):
   - task start module="<module-id>" name="<short title>"

2) After you ask the Gate question and the user answers:
   - If YES: run  task gate yes
   - If NO:  run  task gate no

3) Before declaring DONE you MUST run:
   - task close

If task close fails, you MUST NOT declare DONE.
You MUST update missing artifacts (History/Metrics/Coverage/Expansion memory/Backlog) and retry task close.

Hard rule:
- If there is NO open task in task_state.json, you MUST ask the operator to run task-start and you MUST NOT proceed.

---

# 2) EVERY USER MESSAGE = A NEW TASK (ANTI-SHORTCUT)

Each user instruction is a separate task.

For EACH task you MUST run the FULL cycle.
Even trivial UI edits MUST update:
- module History
- metrics.md
- COVERAGE.md (or explicitly log "no coverage change" in metrics)
- expansion/<module-id>.json
- backlog.md when Gate=NO

You are NOT allowed to do “quick edits” without these updates.

---

# 3) RESOLVER (MANDATORY BEFORE CODE)

1) Read: docs/ai/02-domains/INDEX.yml
2) Resolve the target module using Persian aliases if needed
3) Load module documentation:
   docs/ai/02-domains/<module-id>.md

Collect from frontmatter:
- touches_code
- validation_queries
- depends_on
- smoke_checks
- update_rules
- aliases

Load relevant depends_on docs.

You MUST NOT modify code before resolving documentation.

---

# 4) VALIDATION (DOCS VS REAL CODE)

Before implementation, inspect real project files (as applicable):
- application/app/Http/Controllers/
- application/app/Models/
- application/resources/views/pages/
- application/routes/
- public/js/core/

Answer validation_queries with evidence from code.

If mismatch exists:
- Produce a short Mismatch Report
- Patch documentation FIRST
- Only then continue

Ignoring inconsistency is forbidden.

---

# 5) DISCOVERY MODE (WHEN DOC IS MISSING/UNUSABLE)

Trigger Discovery if:
- module not found in INDEX
- module doc missing
- frontmatter unusable

Follow:
docs/ai/04-docops/DISCOVERY.md

Cursor MUST:
- Identify entry points (route/controller/view/model/assets)
- Follow references (1–2 hops minimum)
- Create/repair module doc + update INDEX.yml
- Add History entry: "Bootstrapped by Discovery"

Only after Discovery may implementation begin.

---

# 6) IMPLEMENTATION RULES

Implementation must be:
- Evidence-driven
- Minimal and incremental
- Patch-oriented

If change affects:
- Data structure
- Persistence
- Business logic
- Permissions
- API contracts

You MUST inspect:
- application/database/migrations/
- application/app/Models/
- application/app/Repositories/
- application/app/Services/

Architectural decisions MUST be recorded in ADRs when needed.

---

# 7) POST-CHANGE LOOP (NON-SKIPPABLE)

After ANY code change, execute ALL steps below.

## 7A) VERIFY
- Re-open touched files and confirm changes
- Validate execution path (controller → view → js) when applicable
- Check 1-hop neighbors for obvious side-effects

## 7B) UPDATE DOCS
Update module documentation:
- Add History entry (date, change, reason, files, impact)
- Update depends_on if needed
- Create/Update ADR if architecture changed
- Maintain bilingual style (Persian explanation, English identifiers)

## 7C) GATE (MANDATORY)
Ask:
"آیا این بخش فعلاً تمام/متوقف است تا گسترش داکیومنت انجام شود؟"

Interpretation:
- YES: run DOC-OPS expansion now
- NO: do NOT run expansion now, BUT still update Metrics/Coverage/Memory and write backlog entry for future expansion.

Then record gate via Guard CLI:
- YES → task gate yes
- NO  → task gate no

## 7D) EXPANSION (ONLY VIA DOC-OPS, IF Gate=YES)
Follow:
docs/ai/04-docops/DOC-OPS.md
Cursor default:
expansion_level = deep

Produce:
- suggested documentation patch
- 3–7 verification questions/tests
- architectural observations

Apply expansion patch ONLY after user approval.

## 7E) METRICS + COVERAGE + MEMORY (MANDATORY)
You MUST update:
- docs/ai/04-docops/metrics.md
- docs/ai/04-docops/COVERAGE.md
- docs/ai/04-docops/expansion/<module-id>.json
- docs/ai/04-docops/backlog.md when Gate=NO

If any file is missing, create a minimal valid version.

---

# 8) GATE + NEW TASK IN SAME MESSAGE (DECONFLICT)

If the user replies YES/NO AND also provides a new task in the same message:

1) FIRST fully close the CURRENT task:
   - Gate record (task-gate-yes/no)
   - required docs/metrics updates
   - task close (must pass)
2) ONLY AFTER closing, start a NEW task cycle from Resolver for the new request.
3) Never treat the new task as a quick edit.

---

# 9) REQUIRED OUTPUT FORMAT (HARD)

For EVERY task response, include these headings (brief is fine):

## RESOLVER
## VALIDATION
## IMPLEMENTATION
## DOCS UPDATE
## METRICS
## GATE
## GUARD CLOSE

If you cannot fill a section, explain why and write a backlog item.

---

# 10) TASK CLOSURE UX (MANDATORY)

After task close succeeds, ALWAYS end with:
"Task closed. Ready for the next task."

Do NOT invent new tasks yourself.

---

# 11) SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH

All architecture/history lives in:
docs/ai/

Never create parallel documentation.
Never bypass Smart Docs.
Never fork history between cursor/local modes.
